  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohammad Samir Azamatullah Shaikh @ ... vs State Of Maharashtra on 26 February, 2026 2026:Bhc-As:10033 Shivgan 11-BA-809-2026.d In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Bail Application No.809 Of 2026 Mohammad Samir Azamatullah Shaikh @ Samir Azamtullah Shaikh ...Appl Versus State of Maharashtra ...",
    "facts": "The case of the prosecution, in brief, is that, on receipt of a secret information, the Police Officials of Kashigaon Police Station intercepted two vehicles. Gutkha substances worth Rs.17,04,586/- were recovered from both the vehicles. The present Applicant was driving Maruti Breeza bearing No.MH- 48/AK-2274. The said vehicle alleged to have used for transportation of Gutkha substance worth Rs.7,81,296/-. Hence, the Applicant came to be arrested on 29th January 2026 pursuant to registration of an FIR. 3. The Applicant filed an application seeking bail before the Additional Sessions Judge, Thane. However, by order dated 12th February 2026, his bail application came to be rejected. Hence, the Applicant is before this Court for the reliefs as prayed. , submits that except the offence punishable under Section 123 of the BNS, all other offences are bailable.",
    "arguments": "It is also submitted that this Court has already held that mere possession, transportation, storage or sale of Pan Masala packets would not attract Section 328 of the IPC (Section 123 of BNS) and the said issue is now pending before the Supreme Court. 5. The Applicant was arrested on 29th January 2026 and has suffered incarceration for about two months. 6. Mr. Mayur Sonavane, learned APP representing the State in the matter, fairly concedes that the matter is pending before the Supreme Court.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "It is also submitted that this Court has already held that mere possession, transportation, storage or sale of Pan Masala packets would not attract Section 328 of the IPC (Section 123 of BNS) and the said issue is now pending before the Supreme Court. 5. The Applicant was arrested on 29th January 2026 and has suffered incarceration for about two months. 6. Mr. Mayur Sonavane, learned APP representing the State in the matter, fairly concedes that the matter is pending before the Supreme Court.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
